<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 120,000 tonnes wheat, 60,000 T barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 120,000 tonnes wheat, 60,000 T barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency said on Thursday it bought 80,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 20,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat, 20,000 tonnes of Australian wheat, 20,000 tonnes of U.S. barley and 40,000 tonnes of Australian barley at its weekly tender.</p>
<p>They are all for September shipment. The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> COUNTRY    QUANTITY</p>
<p> U.S.	 80,000    Western White	    34,000</p>
<p>			    Hard Red Winter</p>
<p>			     (Protein 11.5 pct)    26,000</p>
<p>			    Dark Northern Spring   20,000</p>
<p> Canada     20,000    1CW			  20,000</p>
<p> Australia  20,000    Standard White	   20,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> U.S.	 20,000    Feed			 20,000</p>
<p> Australia  40,000    Feed			 20,000</p>
<p>			    Food			 20,000</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
